From: xxxvik-xakerxxx <xxxviktor.lyskoxxx@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: mediatek: add MT6878 Tetris audio support

Describe the MT6878 audio clocks, AFE, codec and board pinctrl used by
Tetris. Bind the populated AW88261 smart amplifier and start it from the
PCM mute lifecycle, after ASoC has powered the DAPM route. This follows
the Nothing OS 4.1 driver ordering and avoids probing the amplifier PLL
before the I2S clocks are available. Restore the vendor-described
ARMPLL_26M factor as well: without clock ID 171, the generic MediaTek
provider underallocates its onecell table and makes the final FMI2S clock
ID unavailable to the AFE.

---
